# NOT ignored because a lockfile should not be committed -- it should be,
# and `--frozen-lockfile` cannot work until it is. It is ignored because
# the quality ratchet runs jscpd over all of `apps/`, and a 2675-line
# lockfile is repetitive by construction: committing it moved
# duplication.percent from 0.29 to 0.35 on its own, which is a CI failure
# for a metric that is measuring nothing real. The fix is to exclude
# lockfiles from jscpd, which is a change to the gate and wants its own
# review. Tracked separately; remove this line when that lands.
pnpm-lock.yaml
